    "number": 136,
    "title": "Verify bounded standalone cross-device compatibility",
    "body": "Refs #9.\n\nThe reduced personal-project scope needs one compatibility check across the standalone Hub, actual dashboard, Pixoo and Nanoleaf. This adds a bounded synthetic runner using pinned owning source, disposable Linux state and fake physical boundaries. Twelve scenarios cover everyday Codex states, two same-project sessions, one Claude smoke, label/monitor acknowledgment, frontend Nanoleaf settings, MCP Pixoo mode, duplicate/late events, a disconnected consumer and restart without obsolete replay.\n\nThe existing product and UI code are unchanged. The runner checks native queued/applied receipts, current consumer connections, matching freshness and preserved effect epochs. Failed development attempts are recorded in `docs/cross-device-compatibility.md`; the report refuses overwrites and retains preflight failures. The runner rebuilds both TypeScript sources before importing output and forcibly reaps owned process groups when graceful shutdown fails. Both negative checks run in the required Hub CI suite. It reuses existing detailed contract, MCP and migration tests.\n\nLocal validation: Node 24.21.0/Python 3.14.4; 12 source scenarios with cleanup; build/type; 69 Hub tests; 5 dashboard tests and browser/matrix checks; TypeScript/Python controller/lifecycle/state suites; MCP/protocol; packaged Hub; 15 workflow tests; OpenSpec strict validation; guide generation, 5 maintenance tests and browser/print checks. Ten existing specification capabilities remain unchanged; this verification-only change explicitly uses `skip_specs: true`.\n\nGuide inputs and HTML reflect #9's reduced scope and in-progress state. HTML SHA-256: `16b813fe25e7c75307f7faf23cf8056219a2718e45eee7ed63169b0351e705af`. Diagram ownership/flows are unchanged. Public publication is outside scope.\n\nDraft while #30's report in PR #135 awaits delivery. The performance report used its own recorded runtime/pins; it is not relabeled as a timing measurement of #9's settings-capable Nanoleaf revision. Three independent Standards/Specification review rounds resolved all code findings through two correction batches. Final acceptance review after incorporating #30, OpenSpec archive, guarded merge remain pending. All six hosted jobs passed at `48b41a80ebc3fd03ff11206f8bfe10a03a939f00`. No installation, actual agent client, live migration or physical operation occurred.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/136",
