  {
    "number": 135,
    "title": "Qualify everyday standalone monitoring with real consumers",
    "body": "Refs #30.\n\nThe revised personal-project scope needs reproducible standalone source evidence. This adds one confined Linux/WSL qualification command using the delivered hook and Hub, pinned real Pixoo/Nanoleaf consumers, the actual dashboard, and fake Pixoo display transport. It covers one/ten-task monitoring, a short 50-task burst, concurrent integration control, consumer/host outages, restart, retained state and exclusive ownership.\n\nThe retained run at `3f58f2018639a4aff4ce12c6dd3e3dce3d3e0365` passes the predeclared targets: 400 warm events, hook p95 55/73 ms, each consumer receipt p95 below one second, 148 MiB peak Hub RSS, and all 486 hooks below the 3,000 ms hard deadline. Seven development attempts and the failed first full report remain committed. The first full attempt exposed stdout truncation; an awaited report write and 300 KB pipe regression fix it. No target or historical failure was rewritten. Details and raw samples: `docs/performance/standalone-2026-09-22/README.md` and `report.json`.\n\nValidation passed locally on Node 24/Python 3.14: build/type; contract/lifecycle/state and package consumers; MCP/protocol/package/host MCP; Hub/setup/package; dashboard type/unit/browser; baseline performance; workflow; Linux confinement; seven new Python and four new Node checks. Pinned consumer regressions passed 37 Pixoo and 39 Nanoleaf tests. OpenSpec has 11 valid capabilities; the new three-requirement/six-scenario change is synchronized and archived before review.\n\nThe guide's qualification, sequence and recommendation text and complete backlog snapshot are updated, preserving concurrent PRs #131/#134. Generation, five maintenance tests, desktop/mobile/browser/print checks and committed-output drift passed. HTML SHA-256: `e0c5b3753ee8c066d931316df05c33e10df9f6c17e5e583bb17ff340ac3477e2`. No application UI changes; guide edits use the SDLC guide UI exemption. Public publication is outside scope and remains on source `260707019b7ff83d57e31d91ae1e1582c3734589`.\n\nIndependent Standards/Specification review and all six configured PR jobs remain merge gates, followed by merged-main checks before issue closure. This is synthetic source/fake-transport evidence, not installation, actual client, physical or embedded-host qualification. The timing run is local and bounded, not a hosted CI performance gate. Existing CI jobs and baseline limits remain intact.\n",
    "state": "open",
